      "label": "About this example",
      "tool": "Energy & equilibrium",
      "text": "Hydrogenation of ethene: catalysed or not\n\nThe energy profile of C2H4 + H2 → C2H6 with and without a metal catalyst (Pd, Pt, Ni): the catalyst opens a path with a far lower barrier and leaves ΔH unchanged.\n\nUncatalysed: ΔH = -137 kJ/mol, Ea (forward) = 180 kJ/mol, Ea (reverse) = 317 kJ/mol.\nCatalysed (barrier lowered by 150 kJ/mol): Ea = 30 kJ/mol; ΔH is the same, -137 kJ/mol.\nAt 298 K the rate constant is about 1.90e+26 times larger with the catalyst.\nChange \"Barrier lowered by\" or the energies in the table to see the curves move.",
